WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.201
This is a Ozempic.

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:05.205
It's a drug approved by the FDA 
to manage type 2 diabetes.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.740
Maybe you've heard the jingle.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.043
[singing] “Oh, oh, oh Ozempic.”

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.345
Or maybe you've seen Ozempic 
in the news recently

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.646
for another reason.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.981
[overlapping] “Weight loss...”
“... weight loss...”

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:15.915
“Easy weight loss.”

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.017
“Miracle Diet Drug.”

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.785
“Miracle weight loss drug.”

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.320
And it's true.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.354
Ozempic was designed

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.023
to help people manage 
their blood sugar...

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.992
but it's also proven to help 
people lose weight.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:26.960
My doctor was like

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.862
“This is mainly for blood sugar management.”

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.931
“But as a side effects like you will lose weight.”

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.701
When I started to notice that, 
like in the first month or so

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.203
 had dropped 10 pounds,
like nothing.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:39.072
I was like, “There's something 
to this.”

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.540
And once you learn 
why it works

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.308
you'll understand how this drug 

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:46.212
could completely change the way 
we approach weight loss.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.783
According to the latest data from

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.418
the National Institutes of Health

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.553
around 42% of adults 
in the US

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.588
are currently categorized 
as obese.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.825
The CDC's list of health risks 
associated with obesity

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:02.028
include heart disease, stroke, 
and type 2 diabetes...

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.998
diseases that rank among 
the leading causes

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.633
of premature death worldwide.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:10.737
Not everyone living with type 2 diabetes 
is considered obese

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.572
but the two are closely linked.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.141
In fact, one of the leading 
recommendations

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.777
for managing type 2 diabetes 
is weight loss.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.447
Even like a small amount 
of weight reduction

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:23.116
for people with diabetes can help 
blood sugar management.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.551
I'm Mila Clarke.

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:28.088
I'm 33 years old and I have 
a type of diabetes

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:31.057
called latent autoimmune diabetes 
in adults.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.960
I reached out to Mila because 
she runs a YouTube channel...

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.029
Hangry Woman, where she 
makes videos

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.131
about living a healthy life 
with diabetes.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.567
The thing that I wish that 
people understood more

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:45.405
is how difficult it is to live with both 
diabetes and obesity.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:48.108
She's also documented 
her experience with Ozempic.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.843
It has always been really hard for me 

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:52.779
to lose weight despite diet
and exercise

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.081
and paying attention 
to lifestyle habits.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.584
For a long time, doctors 
have had mixed views

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.752
on how to make weight loss 
more accessible...

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.255
to help people lower 
their risk for illnesses

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.556
like type 2 diabetes.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.825
One option is weight loss 
medication.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.761
Historically, weight loss drugs 
have been associated

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.096
with dangerous side effects

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.798
and have been pulled
from the market.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.733
Metabolic bariatric surgery

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.902
is extremely effective 
for weight loss

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.338
but it requires dramatic 
lifestyle changes 

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:20.206
that can be challenging 
to maintain.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.775
But with new diabetes drugs 
like Ozempic...

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:26.312
scientists have a safe and effective 
tool for weight loss...

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:29.883
and it's based on something that's 
inside our bodies and already:

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.318
Hormones.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.387
Hormones are the body's messengers 

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.222
running from one place to another

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.024
prompting certain cells 
into action.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.259
When we eat

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:41.161
our bodies produce 
a bunch of hormones

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.329
to aid in the process 
of digestion.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.165
One of them is GLP-1:

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.333
the hormone that tells us
when we're full.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.203
This is a sequence of amino acids 
that make it up.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:53.840
And this is Semaglutide, the generic name 
for Ozempic.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.142
It's made to mimic GLP-1.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.344
Here's why.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.146
When food enters your stomach

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:02.649
and begins to work its way through 
the digestive system...

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.552
your body releases GLP-1
in the intestine.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:08.888
There are receptors for GLP-1 in cells 
all throughout the body

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.523
that serve different functions 

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.858
when triggered by 
the hormone.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.761
In the pancreas, GLP-1 
receptors

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.529
promote the production 
of insulin

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.631
the hormone that lowers 
blood sugar levels

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.100
and suppress the production 
of glucagon

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.336
the hormone that raises 
blood sugar levels.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.472
This is important for people 
with type 2 diabetes

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.641
whose bodies are insulin resistant

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.810
and produce very little 
insulin of their own.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.413
Synthetic insulin is 
a critical treatment

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.681
for blood sugar management.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.517
And semaglutide makes 
the insulin you do have

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:40.053
whether it's produced naturally
or synthetically

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.588
work better in your body.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.623
Losing excess fat 
can also help you

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.692
become more insulin sensitive.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.095
That's where GLP-1’s next receptor comes in.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:53.132
In the stomach, GLP-1 receptors 
slow gastric emptying...

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.735
which means food doesn't move 
through the digestive system

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.404
as quickly and you stay fuller 
for longer.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:01.140
It slows the digestion 
of your food

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.610
which overall helps with 
blood sugar spikes

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.913
and it helps you feel fuller for longer
so you don't eat as much.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.650
And maybe most importantly, 
at least in regard to weight loss

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.785
there are GLP-1 receptors in the brain...

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.021
particularly in the hypothalamus

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.723
that suppress hunger cravings.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:21.060
That fuller satiety feeling 
for longer is really helpful.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.897
The digestive system is designed 
to do all of this naturally

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:28.501
but GLP-1 based medications are made 
to amplify the hormone’s

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.103
numerous health effects.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.105
And it works.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:35.041
A major clinical trial of 
semaglutide in adults

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:38.244
showed an average weight reduction 
of around 15%

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:41.047
when paired with an adjusted diet 
and exercise routine

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.448
compared to a placebo group,

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.485
which demonstrated a little over 
2% weight reduction.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:48.321
That level of effectiveness 
rivals the results

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.123
of metabolic bariatric surgery.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:51.991
And the fact that I was 
able to take

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:54.027
a once weekly injection
and then all of a sudden

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.461
like the pounds just like dropped off

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.263
I was like, “This is wild to me.”

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.265
These drugs aren't without side effects

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.034
the most common being nausea

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.469
gastrointestinal effects like diarrhea.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.505
Mila initially stopped taking Ozempic

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:08.174
because of a side effect that gave her 
heart palpitations.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.742
But she's back on it now.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.444
And so far, so good.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.745
My blood sugars are great.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.314
I'm having an easier time

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:17.250
losing weight and I've amped up 
my exercise

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:20.153
and being outdoors and hiking 
and running and walking.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.355
And you still have to do 
all of the other things

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:24.824
that everyone has to do 
to be able to lose weight.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.859
It just makes it a little bit easier.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.462
But it's helping me so much with 
my diabetes management.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:33.066
The number of prescriptions 
of Semaglutide has risen dramatically

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.468
since becoming available in late 2017.

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:39.739
And in 2021, the FDA approved
Semaglutide to be prescribed

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:43.076
at a higher dose for weight 
management specifically

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:44.744
branded under the name 
Wegovy.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.613
It was big news and 
led to this drug

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:50.450
getting a lot of attention 
sort of all at once.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.652
The messaging started to center 
more around

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:54.420
weight loss than it did diabetes

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.956
which is unfortunate for 
people with diabetes

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.424
 and people living with obesity.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.959
There are these two groups of people 

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:03.396
who really need this drug 
for health purposes

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:05.131
but it's being trivialized

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.366
and kind of looked at as like

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:08.401
“Oh, this is an easy 
weight loss solution.”

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.036
There are solutions in place now

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.771
to deal with the sudden 
high demand

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.706
for these drugs for people 
who need them.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.975
Mounjaro, another medication 
developed

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.211
specifically for type 2 diabetes

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.313
is currently being fast tracked 
for approval

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.015
by the FDA to be prescribed 
for weight loss too.

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.986
Now that Ozempic’s notoriety helps 
Semaglutide go mainstream

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:29.455
it and drugs like it 
will only become

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.624
more commonly prescribed 
for weight management.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:35.628
It's not as simple as 
“Take this injection

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.897
and you won't be living 
with obesity anymore.”

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:39.999
or “You'll reverse your diabetes.”

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:42.635
But as a community we get 
really excited 

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:44.370
to see innovations happen

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.806
and tools that can make 
our lives a little easier

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:49.909
and that can cause less 
diabetes burn out...

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.311
and helps you think 
about diabetes less.

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:53.846
It's one of those things
that I think...

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.150
all of us want to protect 
at all costs.

